WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.466
Choose your close based on the relationship.

00:00:02.466 --> 00:00:04.932
Soft and hard both have a place.

00:00:04.932 --> 00:00:08.103
This lesson is about soft close vs hard close.

00:00:08.103 --> 00:00:09.512
Choose based on relationship.

00:00:09.512 --> 00:00:11.978
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:15.501
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:20.785
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.785 --> 00:00:24.661
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.661 --> 00:00:28.536
Stay practical: write both closes before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.856 --> 00:00:32.242
A soft close invites a next step without pressure.

00:00:32.242 --> 00:00:34.876
Example: want me to send the one-pager?

00:00:34.876 --> 00:00:37.133
Remember the objective: write both closes.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:41.272
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:41.272 --> 00:00:45.787
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.787 --> 00:00:49.925
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:49.925 --> 00:00:54.440
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.245
A hard close asks for the decision.

00:00:57.245 --> 00:01:00.441
Example: shall we start this week at this price?

00:01:00.441 --> 00:01:02.571
Remember the objective: write both closes.

00:01:02.571 --> 00:01:06.477
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:01:06.477 --> 00:01:10.738
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:01:10.738 --> 00:01:14.643
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:01:14.643 --> 00:01:18.904
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:01:19.224 --> 00:01:20.748
Write both closes now.

00:01:20.748 --> 00:01:23.797
Use soft early, hard when discovery is done.

00:01:23.797 --> 00:01:26.084
Remember the objective: write both closes.

00:01:26.084 --> 00:01:30.276
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:01:30.276 --> 00:01:34.850
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:39.042
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:01:39.042 --> 00:01:43.616
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:01:43.616 --> 00:01:46.284
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:01:46.284 --> 00:01:47.808
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:01:48.128 --> 00:01:50.954
In the quiz, you will write both closes.

00:01:50.954 --> 00:01:55.194
In the quiz, you will practice until you can write both closes.

00:01:55.194 --> 00:01:55.901
Answer carefully.

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:59.080
If you miss one, review the idea and retry.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:03.320
Passing means you can use the concept, not only recognize the words.

